{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFrom Gerrit 1843 PS3 LLM-Review advisories on the RP-04 S2 runtime (e042). Two fail-closed nuances in src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py, both decided by the operator on 2026-08-19 (see approval comment): (1) build_backend is asymmetric — _build_cloud calls assert_cloud_scope_ready at build, but _build_datacenter defers ALL validation to the lazy _LazyDataCenterClient; (2) assert_cloud_scope_ready is deliberately stricter than the legacy ambient assert_env_ready (JIRA_USER-must-be-email, non-empty project), and that tightening is undocumented.\n\n## Approach\nImplement the operator's two approved decisions exactly:\n\n1. **DC build-time non-secret scope assert.** Add `assert_datacenter_nonsecret_scope_ready(scope)` to runtime.py that raises the typed BackendEnvError when the DC base url (`reconciler.base_url`) is empty or the read/write project scope (`jira.project`) is empty — mirroring assert_cloud_scope_ready's project checks. Call it at the top of `_build_datacenter` (same placement as Cloud's assert in `_build_cloud`, before the injected-transport early return). PAT presence and network validation stay lazy in _LazyDataCenterClient / build_client_from_settings, so composing a DC backend still needs neither the [agents]/jira extra nor a JIRA_PAT. The existing full `assert_datacenter_scope_ready` (url + JIRA_PAT, used by JiraDataCenterBackend.assert_env_ready) keeps its behavior and its every-missing-essential-in-one-message property.\n\n2. **Document the stricter Cloud checks as intended.** Extend the assert_cloud_scope_ready docstring (and JiraBackend.assert_env_ready's scope-path note in adapters/jira/backend.py) to state the captured-scope path is DELIBERATELY stricter than the legacy ambient assert_env_ready — the email-format check (Cloud Basic auth requires the account email) and the non-empty-project check (an empty project would query every project) are canonical, an intended tightening, not accidental drift; the legacy ambient path is the compatibility floor.\n\nDefault assumed from the approval: the non-secret assert checks base_url + project/query_project only (never auth_present); it runs even when a test transport is injected, matching Cloud's placement.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py — new assert_datacenter_nonsecret_scope_ready; _build_datacenter calls it; assert_cloud_scope_ready docstring documents the intended tightening.\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py — assert_env_ready docstring: scope path is intentionally stricter (docstring-only).\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py — new fail-closed/lazy-preserved DC build tests.\n\n## Testing\nUnit tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py:\n- happy/lazy path: a DC compose+build with base_url + project set but NO JIRA_PAT still constructs the backend (PAT stays lazy) — run with `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py`.\n- failure path: DC build with empty base_url raises BackendEnvError naming url before any client/transport work; DC build with empty jira.project raises BackendEnvError naming the project scope.\nExisting suites (test_operation_bindings_runtime.py, tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py, DC backend tests) keep passing unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `_build_datacenter` asserts non-secret DC scope readiness (base_url + project) at build via a typed BackendEnvError, verified by the new unit tests failing-closed on empty url/project.\n- [x] A DC backend still composes and builds WITHOUT JIRA_PAT and without the jira extra import at build time, verified by the new lazy-preserved unit test passing with JIRA_PAT unset.\n- [x] assert_cloud_scope_ready's stricter-than-legacy checks (email-format JIRA_USER, non-empty project) are documented in its docstring as an intended, canonical tightening, verified by reading the docstring in the diff.\n- [x] make lint, make typecheck, targeted reconciler tests, and scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check (new=0 increased=0) all pass, verified by running them in the worktree."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787438266877059001,"uuid":"1974b673-0272-4986-aeda-f6780d45c242"}